        <h3 class="text-sm font-black text-gray-950">Aerodynamic Drag &amp; Rolling Resistance</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-2">
        Air density is inversely proportional to temperature. At 15°F (-9°C), air is roughly 12% denser than at 70°F (21°C), significantly increasing aerodynamic drag at speeds above 55 mph. Slushy road surfaces, winter rubber compounds, and underinflated cold tires further increase rolling friction.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

